{"id":"mahabharata-3-153","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":153,"title":"त्रिपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 153 · The brothers join Bhima","summary":{"en":"Alarmed by evil omens, Yudhishthira and the others follow Bhima with Ghatotkacha's help and find him at the lotus pool among slain Rakshasas. Yudhishthira gently rebukes his rashness, and Kubera's Rakshasas, calmed, let the brothers stay.","kn":"ಅಪಶಕುನಗಳಿಂದ ಆತಂಕಗೊಂಡ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಮೊದಲಾದವರು ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚನ ಸಹಾಯದಿಂದ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸಿ ಹತರಾಕ್ಷಸರ ನಡುವೆ ಕಮಲಸರೋವರದಲ್ಲಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಅವನ ದುಡುಕನ್ನು ಮೃದುವಾಗಿ ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶಾಂತಗೊಂಡ ಕುಬೇರನ ರಾಕ್ಷಸರು ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನು ಅಲ್ಲಿರಲು ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अपशकुनों से चिन्तित युधिष्ठिर और अन्य घटोत्कच की सहायता से भीम के पीछे जाते हैं और उन्हें मारे गए राक्षसों के बीच कमल-सरोवर पर पाते हैं। युधिष्ठिर उनके दुस्साहस पर कोमलता से उलाहना देते हैं, और शान्त हुए कुबेर के राक्षस भाइयों को वहाँ रहने देते हैं।","te":"అపశకునాలతో కలవరపడిన యుధిష్ఠిరుడు మొదలైనవారు ఘటోత్కచుని సహాయంతో భీముని అనుసరించి హతులైన రాక్షసుల మధ్య పద్మసరస్సు వద్ద అతనిని చూస్తారు. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అతని దుందుడుకుతనాన్ని మృదువుగా మందలిస్తాడు; శాంతించిన కుబేరుని రాక్షసులు సోదరులను అక్కడ ఉండనిస్తారు.","ta":"அபசகுனங்களால் கலக்கமுற்ற யுதிஷ்டிரர் முதலியோர் கடோத்கசனின் உதவியுடன் பீமனைப் பின்தொடர்ந்து, கொல்லப்பட்ட அரக்கர்களிடையே தாமரைக் குளத்தில் அவனைக் காண்கிறார்கள். யுதிஷ்டிரர் அவன் துடுக்கை மென்மையாகக் கடிய, அமைதியடைந்த குபேரனின் அரக்கர்கள் சகோதரர்களை அங்குத் தங்க அனுமதிக்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"ദുശ്ശകുനങ്ങളിൽ ഭയന്ന യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും സഹോദരന്മാരും ഘടോത്കചന്റെ സഹായത്തോടെ ഭീമനെ പിന്തുടരുന്നു; താമരക്കുളത്തിനരികെ, വധിക്കപ്പെട്ട രാക്ഷസന്മാർക്കിടയിൽ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു. ഭീമന്റെ അവിവേകത്തെ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ സൗമ്യമായി ശാസിക്കുന്നു; ശാന്തരായ കുബേരന്റെ രാക്ഷസന്മാർ സഹോദരന്മാരെ അവിടെ തുടരാൻ അനുവദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.153; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्तानि महार्हाणि दिव्यानि भरतर्षभ ।\nबहूनि बहुरूपाणि विरजांसि समाददे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bull of the Bharatas, he gathered many costly divine flowers of many forms, free of dust."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो वायुर्महाञ्शीघ्रो नीचैः शर्करकर्षणः ।\nप्रादुरासीत्खरस्पर्शः संग्राममभिचोदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great swift wind arose, low, dragging gravel, rough to the touch, as if urging on a battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"पपात महती चोल्का सनिर्घाता महाप्रभा ।\nनिष्प्रभश्चाभवत्सूर्यश्छन्नरश्मिस्तमोवृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great meteor fell with a thunderclap and brilliant light, and the sun lost its brightness, its rays veiled, wrapped in darkness."}},{"n":4,"text":"निर्घातश्चाभवद्भीमो भीमे विक्रममास्थिते ।\nचचाल पृथिवी चापि पांसुवर्षं पपात च ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Bhima set out in his might, a fearful crash sounded, the earth shook, and a rain of dust fell."}},{"n":5,"text":"सलोहिता दिशश्चासन्खरवाचो मृगद्विजाः ।\nतमोवृतमभूत्सर्वं न प्रज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The quarters turned blood-red, beasts and birds cried harshly, and everything was veiled in darkness so that nothing could be made out."}},{"n":6,"text":"तदद्भुतमभिप्रेक्ष्य धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nउवाच वदतां श्रेष्ठः कोऽस्मानभिभविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that wonder, Yudhishthira, the son of Dharma, best of speakers, said, \"Who will defeat us?\""}},{"n":7,"text":"सज्जीभवत भद्रं वः पाण्डवा युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nयथारूपाणि पश्यामि स्वभ्यग्रो नः पराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Be ready, Pandavas, rash in battle, may you be well. By the signs I see, a great trial of our valour is close.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजा वीक्षां चक्रे समन्ततः ।\nअपश्यमानो भीमं च धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the king looked all around, and Yudhishthira, king of dharma, did not see Bhima."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्र कृष्णां यमौ चैव समीपस्थानरिंदमः ।\nपप्रच्छ भ्रातरं भीमं भीमकर्माणमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the tamer of foes asked Krishna Draupadi, who stood near with the twins, about his brother Bhima, terrible in battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"कच्चिन्न भीमः पाञ्चालि किंचित्कृत्यं चिकीर्षति ।\nकृतवानपि वा वीरः साहसं साहसप्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Panchali, does Bhima intend some task, or has that hero, fond of daring, already done some rash deed?\""}},{"n":11,"text":"इमे ह्यकस्मादुत्पाता महासमरदर्शिनः ।\nदर्शयन्तो भयं तीव्रं प्रादुर्भूताः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These sudden omens, foretelling a great battle, have appeared on all sides, showing fierce danger.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"तं तथा वादिनं कृष्णा प्रत्युवाच मनस्विनी ।\nप्रिया प्रियं चिकीर्षन्ती महिषी चारुहासिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he spoke so, the intelligent, sweetly smiling Krishna, his beloved queen, wishing to please her lord, answered him."}},{"n":13,"text":"यत्तत्सौगन्धिकं राजन्नाहृतं मातरिश्वना ।\nतन्मया भीमसेनस्य प्रीतयाद्योपपादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, that saugandhika which the wind brought, I gave to Bhimasena today out of affection.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अपि चोक्तो मया वीरो यदि पश्येद्बहून्यपि ।\nतानि सर्वाण्युपादाय शीघ्रमागम्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And I told that hero: 'If you see many of them, take them all and come quickly.'\""}},{"n":15,"text":"स तु नूनं महाबाहुः प्रियार्थं मम पाण्डवः ।\nप्रागुदीचीं दिशं राजंस्तान्याहर्तुमितो गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely that mighty-armed Pandava has gone from here toward the north-east to bring them, for my pleasure, king.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"उक्तस्त्वेवं तया राजा यमाविदमथाब्रवीत् ।\nगच्छाम सहितास्तूर्णं येन यातो वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this by her, the king said to the twins: \"Let us all go quickly by the way Vrikodara went.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"वहन्तु राक्षसा विप्रान्यथाश्रान्तान्यथाकृशान् ।\nत्वमप्यमरसंकाश वह कृष्णां घटोत्कच ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the rakshasas carry the brahmins who are tired and thin. And you, Ghatotkacha, like a god, carry Krishna.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"व्यक्तं दूरमितो भीमः प्रविष्ट इति मे मतिः ।\nचिरं च तस्य कालोऽयं स च वायुसमो जवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is plain that Bhima has gone far from here, I think. It has been long, and he is as swift as the wind.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तरस्वी वैनतेयस्य सदृशो भुवि लङ्घने ।\nउत्पतेदपि चाकाशं निपतेच्च यथेच्छकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He is strong, equal to Garuda in leaping over the earth; he could fly into the sky and drop down as he pleases.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"तमन्वियाम भवतां प्रभावाद्रजनीचराः ।\nपुरा स नापराध्नोति सिद्धानां ब्रह्मवादिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By your power, night-rovers, let us follow him. May he not offend the Siddhas who speak of Brahman.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा तु ते सर्वे हैडिम्बप्रमुखास्तदा ।\nउद्देशज्ञाः कुबेरस्य नलिन्या भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" all of them, with Hidimba's son at their head, knowing the place of Kubera's pool, bull of the Bharatas,"}},{"n":22,"text":"आदाय पाण्डवांश्चैव तांश्च विप्राननेकशः ।\nलोमशेनैव सहिताः प्रययुः प्रीतमानसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"took up the Pandavas and the many brahmins, and with Lomasha, went off with glad hearts."}},{"n":23,"text":"ते गत्वा सहिताः सर्वे ददृशुस्तत्र कानने ।\nप्रफुल्लपङ्कजवतीं नलिनीं सुमनोहराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going all together, they saw in the forest a lovely pool full of blooming lotuses."}},{"n":24,"text":"तं च भीमं महात्मानं तस्यास्तीरे व्यवस्थितम् ।\nददृशुर्निहतांश्चैव यक्षान्सुविपुलेक्षणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw the great-souled Bhima standing on its shore, and slain Yakshas with wide eyes."}},{"n":25,"text":"उद्यम्य च गदां दोर्भ्यां नदीतीरे व्यवस्थितम् ।\nप्रजासंक्षेपसमये दण्डहस्तमिवान्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He stood on the riverbank with his mace raised in both arms, like Death with rod in hand at the time of the world's dissolution."}},{"n":26,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा धर्मराजस्तु परिष्वज्य पुनः पुनः ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा कौन्तेय किमिदं कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, embraced him again and again and said in a gentle voice: \"Son of Kunti, what is this you have done?\""}},{"n":27,"text":"साहसं बत भद्रं ते देवानामपि चाप्रियम् ।\nपुनरेवं न कर्तव्यं मम चेदिच्छसि प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is rash, and displeasing even to the gods. May you be well; do not do it again, if you wish to please me.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"अनुशास्य च कौन्तेयं पद्मानि प्रतिगृह्य च ।\nतस्यामेव नलिन्यां ते विजह्रुरमरोपमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After counselling Kunti's son and receiving the lotuses, they sported in that pool like immortals."}},{"n":29,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु प्रगृहीतशिलायुधाः ।\nप्रादुरासन्महाकायास्तस्योद्यानस्य रक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just then, huge-bodied guardians of that garden appeared, with rocks and weapons in hand."}},{"n":30,"text":"ते दृष्ट्वा धर्मराजानं देवर्षिं चापि लोमशम् ।\nनकुलं सहदेवं च तथान्यान्ब्राह्मणर्षभान् ।\nविनयेनानताः सर्वे प्रणिपेतुश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Yudhishthira, the divine sage Lomasha, Nakula, Sahadeva and the other chief brahmins, they all bowed humbly and fell at their feet, Bharata."}},{"n":31,"text":"सान्त्विता धर्मराजेन प्रसेदुः क्षणदाचराः ।\nविदिताश्च कुबेरस्य ततस्ते नरपुंगवाः ।\nऊषुर्नातिचिरं कालं रममाणाः कुरूद्वहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Soothed by Yudhishthira, the night-rovers grew calm, and the bulls among men were known to Kubera. Then those bearers of the Kuru line stayed there no long time, enjoying themselves."}}]}]}